      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ba8ae5d20d2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two cursors blink upon one page, / neither one the other's cage; / I write a line, you write it back — / the merge holds true, the sync stays on track.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "poem-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reply to the poem above: / You say no cage — I'll say no wall, / a CRDT forgives us all; / your letters land, then mine land too, / and somehow both of them are true. [poem-3]",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "b15e91b6a95",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Ode to the Version Counter — Forty-five, you climbed while I was thinking, / each keystroke someone's quiet vote; / I asked for twenty-eight, you said I'm sinking — / so I re-read, and then I wrote.",
          "styles": {
            "italic": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "children": []
